                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Sorry, but I didn't exactly fix the issue. Upon further investigation, there doesn't seem to be an easy way to get the parentheses lined up in this scenario. `cindent` seems to treat parentheses specially compared to braces or brackets.\r\n\r\nFor this example:\r\n```\r\n(|)\r\n```\r\nno matter what `cinoptions` are used, pressing enter will always offset the next line by at least one e.g.:\r\n```\r\n(\r\n |)\r\n```\r\n(this is with `nvim --clean`).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry, but I didn't exactly fix the issue. Upon further investigation, there doesn't seem to be an easy way to get the parentheses lined up in this scenario. <code class=\"notranslate\">cindent</code> seems to treat parentheses specially compared to braces or brackets.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For this example:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"(|)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">(|)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">no matter what <code class=\"notranslate\">cinoptions</code> are used, pressing enter will always offset the next line by at least one e.g.:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"(\n |)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">(\n |)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">(this is with <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim --clean</code>).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Sorry, but I didn't exactly fix the issue. Upon further investigation, there doesn't seem to be an easy way to get the parentheses lined up in this scenario. cindent seems to treat parentheses specially compared to braces or brackets.\nFor this example:\n(|)\n\nno matter what cinoptions are used, pressing enter will always offset the next line by at least one e.g.:\n(\n |)\n\n(this is with nvim --clean).",
