                    "body": "> no matter what `cinoptions` are used, pressing enter will always offset the next line by at least one e.g.:\r\n\r\nTechnically, this offset can be removed by `vim.o.cindent = false`. But it seems to block any possible value of 'cinoptions'. As I said, C is treated very special in Vim and Neovim :(\r\n\r\nIf you happen to find a solution, please let me know.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">no matter what <code class=\"notranslate\">cinoptions</code> are used, pressing enter will always offset the next line by at least one e.g.:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Technically, this offset can be removed by <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.o.cindent = false</code>. But it seems to block any possible value of 'cinoptions'. As I said, C is treated very special in Vim and Neovim :(</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you happen to find a solution, please let me know.</p>",
